% ADJ52 case-25 program (this patient's observations + queries only; no rules).
% 63yo man, 45 pack-years, arc-welder of IRON AND STEEL in a poorly ventilated
% bay for the previous several months. Productive cough ~6 weeks; treated as CAP
% with ~3 weeks IV broad-spectrum antibiotics with NO response. Well-appearing,
% afebrile, SpO2 97% RA, PaO2 73 (mildly low), spirometry normal. Prior CXR 3
% months earlier read clear. Current imaging: RUL peribronchial peripheral
% SEGMENTAL air-space consolidation + small ill-defined nodules + background
% centrilobular emphysema. Bronchoscopy: NO endobronchial lesion. BAL: MARKED
% alveolar-macrophage predominance, scant neutrophils/lymphocytes/eosinophils.
% CT-guided needle biopsy: NO malignant cells, NO vasculitis. ANCA negative.
% NOT yet done: Perls' Prussian blue (iron) stain of the BAL/biopsy.

% --- the occupational exposure (the central clue) ---
observe occupational_exposure(iron_steel_arc_welding)
observe exposure_condition(poorly_ventilated)
observe smoking_burden(heavy_pack_years)

% --- the non-resolving consolidation gestalt ---
observe consolidation_response_to_antibiotics(none)
observe general_appearance(well_afebrile)
observe air_space_consolidation(segmental_right_upper_lobe)
observe prior_film(recent_clear)

% --- imaging detail ---
observe ct_pattern(small_ill_defined_nodules)

% --- BAL: macrophage-predominant, scant eosinophils ---
observe bal_pattern(alveolar_macrophage_predominant)
observe bal_eosinophils(scant)

% --- procedures: clean airway, negative tissue, negative serology ---
observe bronchoscopy(no_endobronchial_lesion)
observe biopsy(no_malignant_cells)
observe biopsy(no_vasculitis)
observe biopsy(no_specific_diagnostic_feature)
observe serology(anca_negative)

% NOT observed (open, decision-relevant): iron_stain(...) — the Perls' Prussian
% blue result is pending and is the decisive confirmatory discriminator.

% --- queries: each candidate diagnosis + the recommended next steps ---
? diagnosis(pulmonary_siderosis)
? diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
? diagnosis(lung_adenocarcinoma)
? diagnosis(pulmonary_tuberculosis)
? diagnosis(chronic_eosinophilic_pneumonia)
? diagnosis(anca_vasculitis)
? next_step(prussian_blue_iron_stain_of_bal_and_biopsy)
? next_step(surgical_lung_biopsy)
